A||||4||Pretender||Mechanical oil pressure gauge install?||||5||
Z||000000||Pretender||05-23-2000||01:11 AM||||I've got a sport comp oil pressure gauge and want to install in in my gauge pod, So where do I connect the steel braided line coming from the gauge to the engine? thanks..||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-23-2000||01:27 AM||||Is your engine a V-6 or a 4cyl? I know on my 86 V-6, The oil sending unit is located near the front of the engine on top. you might be able to get a "T" fitting to hook it in. I am not sure if the oil sending unit has any input to the ECM. Logic would tell me it does not but I don't know for sure. So you could just replace the sender with the line. You would lose the oil light and factory gage (if your car has one)||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||05-23-2000||06:58 AM||||I don't know about a V6 but the 4 cyl (at least in the 1984) used a switch activated by oil pressure as an alternate way to turn on the fuel pump.<P>There are rubber disks in the plastic part of the firewall behind the ECM. I installed a mechanical temp gage by running the line through a little hole I punched in one of those rubber disks and then sealing around it with RTV. I then ran the line under the trim up to the radio pod - between the rug and center console.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||triker||05-23-2000||01:49 PM||||I have a SW oil pressure gauge with sender teed off the bottom of the stock sender.  I would take the mechanical line along side the gas tank and bring it up into the front storage area, then through to the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pretender||05-25-2000||02:23 AM||||it's an 88gt, my factory gauge doesn't work so in comes the sport comp from autometer, i have a custom made dual pod piller that it's going into. So the factory sending unit is where? do you mean the front of the engind twords the firewall or the trunk, all depends on which way your facing?..||||reg||1
